back to business.

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:16.943 align:start position:0%
- So what are you thinking
about all this leadership stuff?

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.645
We were at the Senate
building yesterday,

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:20.280
I talked to a couple
of Congress people,

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.015 align:start size:84% position:16%
everyone's jockeying
for position.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:24.117
Tim Scott, Florida, Tim Scott,

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:27.520 align:start position:0%
Senator is now gonna run against
McConnell for the Senate.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:28.988 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, what do you
think is going on here?

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Man, I think it's good,
I think it's healthy.

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:35.328
Look, Mitch has been senate
leader for what, 10 years?

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:36.996 align:start size:84% position:16%
- 75 years, I think.
- I don't know.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:38.998
- It's been a long time.

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:40.500
- He's also 80 years old.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.335
- You know, I don't really

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:43.970
get too caught up
in the age stuff.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:47.173
To me it's are you
have the ability,

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.475
the energy to do the job?

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:50.643
And as long as you
keep that standard,

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:53.480
I'm fine with how old you are
or frankly how young you are.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.014
Because I think sometimes
up here on Capitol Hill,

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:56.916 align:start size:88% position:13%
people are like, "Oh,
well you just got here",

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:58.885
or, "Oh, you're really young."

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:00.153
You know, the Bible always says,

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:01.754
"Don't despise a man
because of his youth."

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.356 align:start size:84% position:16%
So I think it's really
about competence

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.191
and ability and execution.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.293
It's good that Mitch
is getting challenged.

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:08.828
I know that people
tend to be like,

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:10.430
"Oh, well, how could you?"

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:11.898
Well, how could I what?

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:13.366
Every Republican

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:15.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
or every Democrat for
that matter that's up here

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:19.339
is because your people sent
you, they chose to elect you.

00:02:19.339 --> 00:02:21.674
So if people, if we have
to go through that process

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:23.309
and battle for votes at home

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:26.913
and earn the support
every time from voters,

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:29.616 align:start size:97% position:3%
then we come up here, we think
it's all for acclimation.

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:30.850
I think that's wrong.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:32.285
And that's one of
the reasons why

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:34.587 align:start size:81% position:19%
leadership frankly
in both parties

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:37.724
has caused issues for
the people of America.

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:38.892
So I think it's healthy.

00:02:38.892 --> 00:02:40.160 align:start size:84% position:16%
- You must be
feeling pretty good

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.995
about leadership in
Florida these days,

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:44.964
I mean, obviously we were
together on election night.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.799
DeSantis crushes
it by 20 points,

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:49.369 align:start size:88% position:13%
Rubio wins by 15 points,
something like that.

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:52.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like super majority in
the house for Republicans.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.641 align:start size:84% position:16%
We're doing something
right in Florida.

00:02:54.641 --> 00:02:57.010
Is that the blueprint for the
rest of the country right now?

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:57.844
- It is.

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.379
Let's take a step back,

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:00.580
people need to understand
in Florida a couple things,

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.016 align:start size:88% position:13%
one, we have term limits
in our legislature.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:04.484
So you don't have a situation

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:05.952
where you have members
who have just been around

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:09.422 align:start size:97% position:3%
for a long, long time and
then their own power structure

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:11.858
becomes the navigation
point of your state.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.193 align:start size:84% position:16%
(laughing)
Kinda like it is here.

00:03:13.193 --> 00:03:15.695 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Our legislative seats

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:17.797 align:start size:88% position:13%
roll over all the time,
that's number one.

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:20.333
Number two, everybody
knows Ron DeSantis.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:21.968 align:start size:84% position:16%
Let's talk Rick
Scott for a moment.

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:23.603 align:start size:72% position:28%
- Yeah.
- Rick Scott,

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:26.472 align:start size:84% position:16%
before he became
governor Rick Scott,

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:28.474 align:start size:84% position:16%
challenger to Mitch
McConnell, Rick Scott,

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:32.312
he was a donor and
he was a businessman.

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:34.914
Completely upset the apple
cart and the Republican party

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.849
going back what, 2010?

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:39.018
2010, 2012 was the
time when he came in,

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.220
yeah, I think it was 2010.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:41.888 align:start size:84% position:16%
He completely upset
the apple cart.

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:44.791 align:start size:97% position:3%
The Republican establishment
did not want Rick Scott.

00:03:44.791 --> 00:03:47.827 align:start position:0%
He thought that there was a
better way, he becomes governor.

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:50.129 align:start size:81% position:19%
And so then you
have Ron DeSantis.

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:52.899 align:start size:97% position:3%
He was not the establishment's
choice in Florida,

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.400
he becomes governor.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.835 align:start size:81% position:19%
The disruption.
- He was basically

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:56.970
a tea party guy.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:57.937
The Liberty Caucus.

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.205
- He's a freedom caucus.

00:03:59.205 --> 00:04:01.207
One of the Freedom
Caucus founders,

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:04.477 align:start size:88% position:13%
tea party conservative,
tea party patriot.

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:05.712
Now he's governor

00:04:05.712 --> 00:04:07.313
and everybody says now
he's America's governor.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:08.982 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know I said that
first by the way.

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:10.283 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'll just put that out.
- Was that you?

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:11.584
Was that you?
- That was me.

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.453
- But anyway, but
he's basically,

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:14.821 align:start size:84% position:16%
he's the best governor
in the country.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.089
We all know this.

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.890
That is because in Florida,

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:20.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
our political environment
is a meritocracy.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.929 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Mm-hmm.
- That needs to be translated

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:24.664
throughout the United States.

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:27.300
- Do you think other
Red state governors

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.003
have the cahones
basically to do it?

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:31.904
I mean, he picks
the right fights,

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.406
he's bringing in
the right people.

00:04:33.406 --> 00:04:35.041 align:start size:97% position:3%
I always tell people, you
know, from the staff I meet,

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:36.309
it's like these are good people,

00:04:36.309 --> 00:04:38.811 align:start size:84% position:16%
but other governors,
they kind of,

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:40.580
they still want the
media to like them,

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.882 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, he bans mainstream
media from events.

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:45.551
Like he's fighting in a
completely different way.

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:48.454
- I don't know, I always
tell people back home,

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.523
we have a lot of electeds, we
don't have a lot of leaders.

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:52.492 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's just the
truth of the matter.

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:54.093
Carrie Lake,

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:56.996 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, it's unfortunate she
didn't get across the line,

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:59.632 align:start size:97% position:3%
but she was in that mold where
she was just gonna be like,

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:00.633
this is what we're doing.

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:03.236
You either like it or you don't,

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:05.872 align:start size:97% position:3%
but it is what needs to happen
for the state of Arizona.

00:05:05.872 --> 00:05:08.107
And I think that Arizona,
in my view, is gonna suffer

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:09.709 align:start size:97% position:3%
because they're not gonna
have that type of leadership

00:05:09.709 --> 00:05:12.812 align:start position:0%
which is critical in that state
and frankly in all states.

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:15.982
But are other people capable
of Ron DeSantis type leadership

00:05:15.982 --> 00:05:17.650
or Donald Trump type leadership?

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:18.885
- Yeah.

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:20.320
- I think so.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:23.556 align:start position:0%
But you have to have an ability
to not be concerned about

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:25.758 align:start size:84% position:16%
what the pundit
class is gonna think.

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:28.695
You have to be willing to go
against the grain sometimes

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:31.097
because you have to look at
the facts, look at the data

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:33.399
and then present the
best option for people,

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:35.568
regardless of what the
apparatus is gonna say,

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:37.804 align:start size:84% position:16%
regardless of what the
press is gonna say.

00:05:37.804 --> 00:05:41.541
- So you mentioned Trump,
now you're a Trump guy.

00:05:41.541 --> 00:05:43.076 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah.
- And you're a DeSantis guy.

00:05:43.076 --> 00:05:45.478
You know, it seems like
everyone's just itching

00:05:45.478 --> 00:05:46.879
for this fight.

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:49.782 align:start size:97% position:3%
Trump's thrown out a
couple lines on this thing.

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:51.017
I keep telling my audience,

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:52.485
look, I feel like
I win either way

00:05:52.485 --> 00:05:54.887
because if DeSantis doesn't run,

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:56.723
he's our governor and
that's freaking great

00:05:56.723 --> 00:05:58.024
and then I'll support Trump.

00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:00.493 align:start size:84% position:16%
If they both run,
they'll battle it out,

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:01.961 align:start size:84% position:16%
and hopefully it
doesn't get too nasty

00:06:01.961 --> 00:06:03.496
and we get a better
candidate out of it.

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:05.565
But what do you
think for people,

00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:07.367
'cause I think a lot of
people like 'em both,

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:09.936
partly for the same reasons,
partly for different reasons.

00:06:09.936 --> 00:06:11.504
Where does that put you

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:14.207 align:start size:84% position:16%
and what do you think
they need to do?

00:06:14.207 --> 00:06:15.708
How about that?

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:18.277
- First and foremost, does
it put me in a bad spot?

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:19.445
Oh yeah.

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:21.914 align:start size:88% position:13%
Because look, I'm
supportive of both men.

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:23.916
They both have been tremendous

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:25.418
in the roles that they've played

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:26.886
in the apparatus
of our politics.

00:06:26.886 --> 00:06:28.821
Donald Trump speaks for itself,

00:06:28.821 --> 00:06:30.022
our country, and frankly,

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:32.759 align:start size:84% position:16%
Republicans learned
how to stand up

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:35.061
and do the right thing
because of Donald Trump.

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:36.662
- Simply would not have
happened without him.

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:37.497
- Absolute truth.

00:06:37.497 --> 00:06:38.431
- Say what you want,

00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:39.632
but whether it's Mitt Romney,

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:41.300
John McCain, God rest his soul,

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:45.004
George W. Bush, we
had seen the line of

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:46.873
let's just try to do the
things that are possible,

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:48.074
be leery of the press

00:06:48.074 --> 00:06:50.109 align:start size:84% position:16%
'cause they have
more ink in their pen

00:06:50.109 --> 00:06:51.444 align:start size:84% position:16%
than you have
words in your mouth

00:06:51.444 --> 00:06:52.912
and all that kind
of other stuff.

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:54.414 align:start size:84% position:16%
And Donald Trump broke
that mold and said,

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:55.948
"No, forget all that.

00:06:55.948 --> 00:06:57.450
Those people don't even know
what they're talking about.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:07:00.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do the job and then let
the people see the results

00:07:00.486 --> 00:07:01.821
and they'll reward you."

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:03.322
And so he has,

00:07:03.322 --> 00:07:06.359
really he is the catalyst for
the new wave of Republican.

00:07:06.359 --> 00:07:09.562
But if you're gonna ask me
what I think needs to happen,

00:07:09.562 --> 00:07:12.432 align:start size:97% position:3%
Donald Trump's speech
announcing for the presidency

00:07:12.432 --> 00:07:14.634
was exactly where
he needs to be.

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:15.468
- Yeah.

00:07:15.468 --> 00:07:16.302
The tone was right.

00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:17.804
- Pitch perfect.

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:21.441 align:start size:97% position:3%
Talking about his agenda and
talking about his record.

00:07:21.441 --> 00:07:24.010
Because beyond a
shadow of a doubt,

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:26.512
he has the very best record

00:07:26.512 --> 00:07:29.182
of anybody in the United States.

00:07:29.182 --> 00:07:31.551 align:start size:81% position:19%
Stay in that lane,
focus on that.

00:07:31.551 --> 00:07:33.319
He's the leader
in the clubhouse.

00:07:33.319 --> 00:07:36.289 align:start size:97% position:3%
If that's the Donald Trump you
see for the next 16 months,

00:07:36.289 --> 00:07:37.890
he's president of
the United States.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.525
You can go ahead and
book that right now.

00:07:39.525 --> 00:07:40.993
- What would you want to happen

00:07:40.993 --> 00:07:43.362 align:start size:97% position:3%
between him and the governor
if the governor gets in?

00:07:43.362 --> 00:07:44.764
I know it's a little
hypothetical stuff,

00:07:44.764 --> 00:07:46.365
but how would you
want it to go down?

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:47.567
I mean, you know, both of them,

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:49.202 align:start size:84% position:16%
do you want it to
all be done publicly?

00:07:49.202 --> 00:07:52.171 align:start position:0%
Do you want them to kind of
have the sit down at Mar-a-Lago.

00:07:52.171 --> 00:07:54.607 align:start size:81% position:19%
and figure out how
to work it out?

00:07:54.607 --> 00:07:56.075
- I mean, look, I would hope
they would have a sit down

00:07:56.075 --> 00:07:57.610
and figure this thing out,

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:58.978
whether that's Mar-a-Lago
or the governor's mansion,

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:00.313
whatever that other place is.

00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:02.682
Something tells me to.
- They're too Trump.

00:08:02.682 --> 00:08:04.484
- They might wanna
do it in Orlando,

00:08:04.484 --> 00:08:06.519
somewhere neutral site or
whatever, I don't know.

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:08.588
But I would hope that
they would work it out.

00:08:08.588 --> 00:08:10.890
Now the reality in politics is

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:12.592
sometimes that's
