working in concert with them.

00:13:12.291 --> 00:13:13.793
Everybody is pulling forward.

00:13:13.793 --> 00:13:15.461
It's just gonna take
time to get it back.

00:13:15.461 --> 00:13:17.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Were there any major
screw ups with this thing?

00:13:17.396 --> 00:13:20.766
'Cause it felt like it was
just as disastrous as it was

00:13:20.766 --> 00:13:22.468
that it was just kind
of clean and obviously,

00:13:22.468 --> 00:13:23.736 align:start size:88% position:13%
the governor gets a
lot of credit for that,

00:13:23.736 --> 00:13:25.237
but FEMA,

00:13:25.237 --> 00:13:26.705
there are federal agencies
that came in and helped too.

00:13:26.705 --> 00:13:28.407
- Well, listen, first of
all, in terms of screw ups,

00:13:28.407 --> 00:13:30.109 align:start size:88% position:13%
the way the press
likes to talk about it.

00:13:30.109 --> 00:13:31.343 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Well, 'cause
they were waiting,

00:13:31.343 --> 00:13:32.545 align:start size:84% position:16%
they wanted something.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:13:32.545 --> 00:13:33.479 align:start size:84% position:16%
- This is a problem
with the press,

00:13:33.479 --> 00:13:34.713
they do this stuff all the time.

00:13:34.713 --> 00:13:36.448
The reality is that storm,

00:13:36.448 --> 00:13:38.884
and I remember I was at the
National Hurricane Center

00:13:38.884 --> 00:13:42.421 align:start size:97% position:3%
'cause I was here in DC
when the storm made landfall

00:13:42.421 --> 00:13:44.857
and the modelers were
telling me directly,

00:13:44.857 --> 00:13:47.660
it was tough to predict
the track on this storm

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:49.228 align:start size:84% position:16%
because it kept,
they call it jogging,

00:13:49.228 --> 00:13:51.430
like it kept moving from here
to there, to here to there.

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:54.800
And it just kept jogging,
I think it was Tuesday,

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:57.436
late Monday into Tuesday
before that storm hit.

00:13:57.436 --> 00:13:59.572 align:start size:88% position:13%
We had people who
evacuated from Tampa Bay

00:13:59.572 --> 00:14:01.040
in Fort Myers.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:02.408 align:start size:88% position:13%
- And they were shocked
when they basically

00:14:02.408 --> 00:14:04.410 align:start size:84% position:16%
were in the epicenter
of the storm

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:06.345 align:start size:88% position:13%
because all the modeling
had showed Tampa Bay,

00:14:06.345 --> 00:14:08.180
Sarasota County.

00:14:08.180 --> 00:14:10.282
And so that's kind
of what happened.

00:14:10.282 --> 00:14:12.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was tough, but I think
in terms of response,

00:14:12.785 --> 00:14:17.056
in terms of preparedness
and response, top notch.

00:14:17.056 --> 00:14:19.158
- All right, I got
one more for you,

